    HuBrightnessBridge: makes the Android brightness slider drive AOSP Extra Dim,
    because device 3 has no reachable backlight dimmer
    (docs/research/2026-09-10-mcu-backlight-brightness.md). Installed only with
    BENGAL_EXTRA_DIM=1 (device.mk), so with the knob off there is no app and no write.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
          package="com.meinte.hubrightnessbridge">

    <!--
        NO android:sharedUserId, same reasoning as HuButtons/HuRadio: user=system
        would put the app in system_app. With none, a platform-signed priv-app with
        no seapp_contexts line of its own lands in AOSP's platform_app, which is all
        this needs (one ContentObserver, Settings reads/writes via system_server).
    -->

    <!--
        The one permission. It writes the three Settings.Secure reduce_bright_colors
        keys that ColorDisplayService observes. signature|privileged: granted by the
        platform certificate and allowlisted in privapp-permissions for
        ro.control_privapp_permissions=enforce. Reading screen_brightness and the
        @hide keys needs nothing (system app, SettingsProvider enforceSettingReadable).
    -->
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.WRITE_SECURE_SETTINGS" />

    <!--
        persistent: AMS starts it at boot and keeps it alive, which a ContentObserver
        needs. directBootAware: it can start before user unlock; bengal3 has no lock
        screen, but the boot re-assert should not wait for one. No activity, service,
        receiver or provider: nothing to launch and nothing exported.
    -->
    <application
        android:name=".BridgeApplication"
        android:icon="@mipmap/ic_bengal_launcher"
        android:roundIcon="@mipmap/ic_bengal_launcher"
        android:label="Brightness Bridge"
        android:persistent="true"
        android:directBootAware="true"
        android:defaultToDeviceProtectedStorage="true"
        android:allowBackup="false" />

</manifest>
